#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ds41-pair: set up, run and verify the DeepSeek V4.1 Flash pair on two Strix Halo nodes.

Run the same commands on both nodes; each node has its own small config file (rank, peer, model directory, profile).
Every step is idempotent and can be re-run. Nothing here runs as root: steps that need root are printed for you to
run, or run one by one (each shown first) only with an explicit --yes-root.

  ds41-pair init --rank 0 --peer user@node-b --model-dir /path/to/models    write this node's config
  ds41-pair check                     read-only preflight of this node (and the peer over SSH)
  ds41-pair driver [--yes-root]       build the USB4 driver modules for the running kernel, then the root steps
  ds41-pair driver-verify [--link-test]   both cables, link speed, the four streams (and a live exchange)
  ds41-pair build                     build the trellis library and the engine with the production options
  ds41-pair fetch [--dry-run] [--from-peer] [--verify]   pinned weights, every SHA-256 checked, resumable
  ds41-pair prepare [--dry-run]       optional one-time expert preparation (faster model loads)
  ds41-pair run [--both] | stop [--both] | status | logs | unit [--install]
  ds41-pair smoke                     exact token check against the published reference and one speed line

Full guide: docs/pair-setup.md.
"""
